/**
 * @defgroup FstmGeo FstmGeo — Forward Silicon Tracker Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR Forward Silicon Tracker (FST), detector tag FSTM.
 *
 * @details
 * The Forward Silicon Tracker (FST) consists of three annular silicon-strip disk planes
 * located at z = 151.750, 165.248, and 178.781 cm on the east (positive-z) side of STAR.
 * Each disk spans radii from approximately 5 cm to 34 cm, providing track reconstruction in
 * the pseudorapidity range 2.5 < η < 4.  The detector was commissioned as part of the STAR
 * forward upgrade programme for the BES-II and FWD physics campaigns (ca. 2020–present).
 *
 * Each disk is segmented into twelve trapezoidal wedges arranged in two half-rings of six
 * wedges each.  Every wedge carries a silicon strip sensor read out through APV25 hybrid
 * circuits on T-boards, cooled via stainless-steel/Novec liquid-cooling loops embedded in a
 * PEEK and CFRP mechanical structure.
 *
 * Four AGML module variants are provided:
 *   - **FstmGeo** — full production geometry including all material detail (cooling, heat sinks,
 *     hybrids, APV chips, T-boards, support rings, ribs).
 *   - **FstmGeoS** — simplified geometry that merges fine detail into equivalent material
 *     budget volumes; used for fast simulation.
 *   - **FstmGeoM** — full geometry with per-half misalignment parameters read from an
 *     alignment database; intended for systematic studies.
 *   - **FstmGeoSM** — simplified geometry with per-half misalignment; combines the speed
 *     of FstmGeoS with the alignment capability of FstmGeoM.
 *
 * The top-level mother volume FSTM is a tube (rmin = 4.1 cm, rmax = 34.0 cm, dz = 30.0 cm)
 * placed at z = 165 cm.  Each disk container FSTD holds twelve FSTW wedge assemblies; the
 * silicon sensitive layer is FTUS.
 *
 * @par Authors
 * Te-Chuan Huang, Flemming Videbaek
 *
 * @par History
 * - March 2020: Initial AGML module created.
 * - December 2020: Disk z-positions updated to surveyed values from F. Videbaek.
 * - January 2021: Symbolic parameter consolidation; inner support ring added.
 * - June 2021: Middle-ring wedge rotation by 180° to avoid mechanical interference.
 * - July 2021: Disks moved outward by ~5 cm (2 in); inner support tubes removed.
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @defgroup FstmGeoFull FstmGeo — Full Production Geometry
 * @ingroup FstmGeo
 * @brief Complete material description including cooling, heat sinks, APV chips, hybrids,
 *        T-boards, ribs, and both inner and outer mechanical support structures.
 *
 * @details Activated by setup tags @c FSTMon and @c FSTMv1 in FstmConfig.xml.
 * All per-wedge detail volumes (FSHA–FSHH, FHOA–FHOD, FHAE–FHBH heat sinks; FHTS/FCHT/FCHB
 * cooling holders; FSBW ribs; FSWT connecting tubes) are instantiated in full.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup FstmGeoSimplified FstmGeoS — Simplified Geometry
 * @ingroup FstmGeo
 * @brief Reduced-volume geometry preserving total material budget; for fast simulation.
 *
 * @details Activated by setup tag @c FSTMv1s.  Fine structural detail (individual heat sinks,
 * rib sub-volumes, cooling holder tubes) is merged into aggregate material descriptions.
 * Silicon disk z-positions are identical to FstmGeo.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup FstmGeoMisaligned FstmGeoM — Misaligned Full Geometry
 * @ingroup FstmGeo
 * @brief Full geometry variant that applies per-half misalignment from an alignment database.
 *
 * @details Activated by setup tag @c FSTMv1m.  Reads misalignment offsets via the
 * @c wholewedge.modulus2 index array, which maps each wedge to an alignment-database row.
 * Intended for systematic studies of alignment effects on track reconstruction.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup FstmGeoSM FstmGeoSM — Simplified Misaligned Geometry
 * @ingroup FstmGeo
 * @brief Combines the reduced volume set of FstmGeoS with per-half misalignment support.
 *
 * @details Activated by setup tag @c FSTMv1sm.  Provides the fastest simulation option
 * while still accepting alignment corrections from the database.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
